/packages/jido_harness/cover/**
/packages/jido_harness/deps/**/_build/**

# Vendored hex packages (TRD-001 offline `deps/`) ship their own `.credo.exs`,
# and the git index still carries `packages/jido_harness/deps/credo/.credo.exs`
# from the vendoring commit. That file is third-party source, not this repo's
# config, but it is git-VISIBLE, and OMP's `cleanse` checker discovery treats
# every visible `.credo.exs` as a Credo project root: it ran `mix credo` inside
# `packages/jido_harness/deps/credo`, i.e. it tried to lint Credo's own source,
# which fails immediately on Credo's uninstalled dev-only deps (`inch_ex`,
# `mix_test_watch`, `ex_doc`, `file_system`, `bunt`, `jason`) with
# "Unchecked dependencies ... ** (Mix) Can't continue due to errors on
# dependencies". Ignoring the path removes it from the visible set that
# discovery scans (`git ls-files` + `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard`)
# while leaving the blob in history; `git rm --cached` pairs with it, so nothing
# under any `deps/` directory can be mistaken for a project root again. Real
# configs (`packages/foreman_server/.credo.exs`) are untouched and stay visible.
packages/*/deps/**/*.credo.exs
.devbox/

# Stray worktree test-fixture snapshots dropped at repo root by some
# workflow/RunExecutor tests
/.worktrees/
# Foreman/Jobsite-dispatched agents run with the repository root as their cwd,
# so the ensemble tooling's per-run scratch (run index, active locks, working
# plans) lands here. It is machine-local runtime state, never review material:
# jobsite run js-b6e1438582585cf6 committed three such files into a feature
# branch as a side effect of writing the PRD/TRD the run was asked for.
/.ensemble/new-feature/
# Local CI gate (.ensemble/local-ci.yaml): each run clones the PR head into
# .ensemble/local-ci-runs/<sha> and keeps a failing step's full output in
# .ensemble/local-ci-runs/logs. Machine-local, and a nested clone must never be added.
/.ensemble/local-ci-runs/
*.coverdata
